    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d605">

                <pb facs="0594" n="520" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg520"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Perry</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 82.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-03-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 28, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatches No. 173, dated March 8, and
                    No. 174, dated March 10 have been received, and have been submitted for perusal
                    to the Secretary of the Navy.</p>
                <p>The ceaseless vigilance and activity which you have shown in your efforts to
                    protect the interests of the United States, in connexion with the affair of the
                    pirate Stonewall at Ferrol, are especially commended.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Horatio</hi> J, <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Perry,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                            Madrid.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
